{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"3bcba16e5224a7d88e79abc2abab0d326dd7cd07091cd6969f6bbd39eacf8699","packTokens":2430,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":374,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":634,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1101,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Import procurement and receiving data and map PO lines to lots and pens with traceability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Forecast lifecycle milestones, target weights, and projected market dates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Track feed inventory, stock movements, wastage, and forecasts across multiple time horizons.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Create and optimize rations with ingredient proportions, nutritional values, and costs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Generate pen-level feeding plans and schedules using bunk rates, ration, and animal counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Record feeding activities, compare planned and actual quantities, decrement inventory, and roll up lot costs and consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Record dated lot weight measurements and maintain weight trends.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate feed-to-gain metrics, profitability, forecasts, and recommendations from feeding and weight data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide dashboards, reports, filters, and CSV or PDF exports for feedlot operations and performance.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Create mock data and present the proposed architecture, demo, validation, challenges, readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How should ration cost optimization produce candidate mixes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Generate candidate ingredient proportions against user-entered nutrition or animal-range constraints; show the cost and trade-offs, and require a user to save or assign a candidate.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which user roles and permissions should the app enforce?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use Administrator and Operator roles: administrators manage users, imports, and configuration; operators manage plans and record feeding and weights; both can view dashboards and reports.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users sign in to the app?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use administrator-managed email and password accounts; defer SSO and self-service registration.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"When a PO line is split across multiple lots, how should its purchase costs be allocated to each lot’s financial baseline?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allocate costs in proportion to the received animal head count assigned to each lot.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should wastage appear as its own dated inventory movement, or only as a factor in usage and forecasts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Include wastage in the configured consumption estimate and projections, but do not create a separate wastage movement.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the bunk rate be interpreted when generating a pen’s planned feed quantity?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day, multiplied by the planned animal count.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Should feed-to-gain calculations use feed quantities as-fed or adjust them to dry matter?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use as-fed pounds for feed consumption and FCR.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When a pen contains animals from multiple lots, how should a pen-level feeding plan or activity be attributed for lot rollups?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record a separate lot allocation for each portion of the pen’s planned or delivered feed.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build the Feedlot as a responsive web app with administrator-managed email-and-password accounts, Administrator and Operator roles, role-appropriate pages and controls, and synchronized procurement and receiving records from a configured mock source with per-record outcomes, identifiers, and errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Show procurement traceability from PO lines through lots to pens, available procurement and animal fields, pen capacity and animal counts, proportional lot purchase-cost allocations, and Unknown for missing animal sex; show lot lifecycle milestones, target weights, projected market dates, and the measured or configured growth assumption used.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Provide feed inventory entry and views that retain entered units, show normalized calculation values where applicable, and display opening, received, consumed, and closing stock; show daily through annual projections using configured wastage without a separate wastage movement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Allow users to create and view rations with ingredients, proportions, nutrition, intended animal or weight range, and normalized cost per pound while retaining entered units; show ration optimization candidates, costs, and trade-offs, requiring an accepted explicit save or assign action before using a candidate.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Generate dated pen feeding plans with planned quantity calculated from as-fed bunk rate and planned animal count, plan details, and proportional lot allocations; show feeding schedules by date and pen with planned quantity and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Operators to record planned or unplanned feeding activities with lot allocations, and show returned planned and actual quantities, variance when linked, inventory results, cost, energy, status, lot allocations, and rollups, including plan mismatches. Display API-returned consumption and allocations without calculating inventory decrements in the web app; on insufficient-stock refusal retain entered values and show the error without marking the activity saved or updating totals. For accepted edits or cancellations, show returned activity and totals, or the returned error.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Operators to record dated lot weight measurements and show returned measurements in weight history and trends; show lot performance metrics and refresh them after accepted feeding or weight events. Show available purchase and feed costs, feed cost of gain separately, recorded sale revenue and returned broader profitability when available, an unavailable label when ROI data is incomplete, and returned feeding or sale-timing recommendations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an operations dashboard with active lots and pens, operational counts and inventory, ration and plan information, feed and weight performance, energy use, and lot rankings; provide a yard summary with total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a Feed-to-Gain report comparing lot ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, with date-range, breed, known-sex, and pen filters, and CSV or PDF export of displayed report data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a demo and presentation view with mock operational data and materials covering the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, demo flow, coding prompts, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Use responsive layouts for phone, tablet, and desktop, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens; conform main application flows to WCAG 2.1 AA; support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox; use English and left-to-right layout; and build staging and production deployment targets through a pipeline.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}